{
 "name": "eden_bay_map",
 "description": "Old sepia-style map of the far south coast of New South Wales (Eden, Twofold Bay): yellowed cream paper #efe2b8 with aged darker border and foxing spots, brown ink coastline (land on the left, sea on the right), horizontal hatched sea with coastal ripple lines, hill hachures and little trees inland, a compass rose with N at (410,-230), no place names. Twofold Bay is the clear bite in the coast centred on (120,40); the Kiah River winds in from the west and enters its south shore at (100,90). Merimbula/Pambula lagoons at (110,-150) / (150,-60), Green Cape headland (295,215), Cape Howe and the coast turning west at the bottom (235,368). 1100x800, anchor centre.",
